.TH CHTTPSVR_CONSTRUCT_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_construct_scoped \- declare a chttpsvr handle, initialize it, and destroy it automatically
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

chttpsvr_construct_scoped(name, cl);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This macro joins chttpsvr_declare_scoped and a call to
ccol_create_chttpsvr(cl).  It declares name with a GCC cleanup
attribute.  The compiler therefore destroys the server automatically
when name leaves the scope.  It destroys the server in exactly the way
that chttpsvr_destroy does.  On a failure the macro calls
ccol_fatal_err() and does not return.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name     The identifier for the new handle variable.
cl       The parent logger to derive the logger of this server from.
         Pass CLOG_INVALID to use an internal logger that writes only
         FATAL messages to stderr.  See ccol_create_chttpsvr_mp for
         the details.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_construct (3),
.BR chttpsvr_declare_scoped (3)
